      "text": "Health psychology applies psychological science to physical health outcomes.\nThe core insight: stress is not just \"feeling bad\" — it's a physiological\ncascade with measurable immunological, cardiovascular, and neurological\nconsequences. Cohen's cold studies gave us the cleanest human data. McEwen's\nallostatic load gave us the cumulative wear-and-tear framework. Together they\nexplain why ACEs (adverse childhood experiences) shorten life expectancy."
